# class: ci-pipelines
# schema: section | title | kind | summary | source
# source: docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md
# recipe: novel

intro | CI/CD Pipelines - outbound view for this repo | rationale | MVP-CI = build+test+package only; no deploy (CR-0010 §3k); CD deferred until Terraform §4 | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#cicd-pipelines--deployment-dashboard
two-docs | Two CI/CD docs - different concerns | rationale | ci-cd-integration.md = inbound; ci-cd-pipelines.md = outbound (this repo's 4 components -> GHCR) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#1-two-cicd-docs--different-concerns
topology | Topology - four thin callers, one reusable workflow | topology | _build-and-push-image.yml (reusable) + api/fetcher/frontend/gateway.yml callers; build-kind input switches dotnet|static; path-filtered | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#2-topology--four-thin-callers-one-reusable-workflow
topology-component-image | Component -> image -> Dockerfile mapping | reference | Caller-to-image-to-Dockerfile-to-context table for all four components | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#component--image--dockerfile
triggers | Triggers | contract | push-main, tag-v*, pull_request, workflow_dispatch; PR builds without push (fork-safe) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#3-triggers
triggers-concurrency | Concurrency model | contract | concurrency=${{github.workflow}}-${{github.ref}} cancel-in-progress:true (CR-0010 §3i) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#3-triggers
tag-scheme | Tag scheme (Q5) | contract | docker/metadata-action@v5: tag-push -> vX.Y.Z+vX.Y+sha-<7>+latest; main -> sha-<7>+latest; PR -> pr-<N>-sha-<full> (built, not pushed) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#4-tag-scheme-q5
quality-gates | Quality gates | contract | 7-row matrix (gate/severity/mechanism/notes); blocking: backend-format, backend-unit, frontend-unit, mockup-visual; non-blocking artefact: backend+frontend coverage; deferred: frontend-lint (D3 lock) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#5-quality-gates
caching | Caching | contract | 4 tiers (CR-0010 §3g): NuGet, npm, Playwright-browsers, Docker-layers (per-image scope) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#6-caching
ef-migration-artefact | EF migration SQL artefact (api.yml only) | contract | emit-migration-artefact:true; dotnet ef migrations script --idempotent; uploads ef-migrations-script-<sha> (90d retention) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#7-ef-migration-sql-artefact
ef-idempotent-contract | EF script idempotent contract | contract | --idempotent wraps DDL in existence checks; safe to re-apply against any historical schema state; contract future CD relies on | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#7-ef-migration-sql-artefact
ef-generation-only | EF script: generation only, never executed | rationale | Catches missing migrations + model-snapshot conflicts + design-time DbContext failures pre-deploy; uses placeholder ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#7-ef-migration-sql-artefact
ef-download-howto | EF script download | how-to | GitHub -> Actions -> run -> Artifacts -> ef-migrations-script-<sha> | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#7-ef-migration-sql-artefact
manual-rerun | Manual reruns via workflow_dispatch | how-to | All 4 callers expose workflow_dispatch; no inputs; pushes latest+sha-<7> from main, only sha-<7> from non-default branches | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#8-manual-reruns--workflow_dispatch
version-bump | Bumping a version - tag flow | how-to | git tag vX.Y.Z + git push origin vX.Y.Z; fires all 4 workflows + release.yml; tag scheme event-driven (no workflow edits) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#9-bumping-a-version--tag-flow
release-pipeline | Release pipeline - v* tag -> release assets | rationale | Separate .github/workflows/release.yml fires on v* tag push; publishes assets the one-liner installer (issue #7, ADR-0005) consumes; runs alongside the 4 component workflows on the same tag push; outbound in the same sense §1 defines | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#10-release-pipeline--v-tag--release-assets
release-asset-visibility | Asset visibility + fetch auth | contract | Repo + GHCR both private; anonymous fetches return 404; transport-layer choice is GitHub CLI (gh); 4-row surface/auth table covers install.ps1+sh download / docker-compose.release.yml+migration.sql / GHCR image pull / release.yml workflow itself; required gh scope union: read:packages | write:packages | admin:packages; gh auth refresh --scopes read:packages prereq | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#asset-visibility--fetch-auth
release-trigger | Release pipeline trigger | contract | push of tag v* (e.g. v1.2.3) -> release.yml creates GitHub Release + attaches assets; does NOT run on push:main, PRs, or workflow_dispatch from non-tag ref; tag push is sole trigger | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#trigger
release-assets-published | Assets published per release | contract | Six assets per vX.Y.Z release (installer refuses missing): docker-compose.release.yml (image refs templated with ${DASHBOARD_VERSION} at publish), install.ps1 + install.sh (Option A per issue #7, mirrors dev_env/start.ps1 UX, inherits -Fetcher / -Demo precondition matrix), uninstall.ps1 + uninstall.sh (compose down + cleanup), migration.sql (downloaded from same-commit api.yml artefact OR re-generated by release job via dotnet ef migrations script --idempotent) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#assets-published
release-canonical-asset-url | Canonical asset URL | contract | https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/releases/download/<tag>/<asset-name>; durable + immutable per-tag; expected discovery surface (Releases tab); private-repo gated -> gh release download <tag> --repo <owner>/<repo> --pattern <asset-name>; fallback raw GitHub-at-tag URL documented but raw-content also private-gated (gh api repos/.../contents/...?ref=<tag> equivalent); migration.sql NOT mirrored to raw-content path (asset is generated, not committed) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#canonical-asset-url
release-migration-actuation | Migration actuation (release-install) | contract | One-shot migrations service declared in docker-compose.release.yml under migrate profile (ADR-0005): step 1 installer downloads migration.sql -> step 2 docker compose --profile migrate up -d --wait runs psql with ON_ERROR_STOP=1 against db-healthy -> step 3 api waits for migrations:service_completed_successfully (mirrors dev_env/docker-compose.local.yml verbatim); installer applies migrations by DEFAULT (-SkipMigrations / --skip-migrations opts out; URL panel shows yellow notice on unmigrated DB); idempotent-script contract (§7) guarantees re-application is no-op | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#migration-actuation
release-notes | Release notes | how-to | release.yml populates GitHub Release body from CHANGELOG.md (when present) plus auto-generated "Install / upgrade" section pointing at canonical asset URLs; user-facing install surface per issue #7 acceptance criterion "Quick start (release install) section above the contributor-oriented one" | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#release-notes
release-cross-refs | Release pipeline cross-references | links | ADR-0005 (migration actuation decision) + issue #7 (triggering requirement) + issue #5 + install/install.ps1 §1 (-Fetcher / -Demo precondition) + ci-cd-integration.md § Anonymous-mode transport + §7 (migration.sql generation) + §4 (tag scheme) + architecture.md §8 footnote (API_TOKEN install-time generation) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#cross-references
ghcr-to-acr | GHCR -> ACR cutover (Q4 deferred) | future | When Terraform §4 lands: change registry input + swap docker/login-action GHCR for azure/login@v2 + docker/login-action ACR (OIDC); tag scheme registry-agnostic | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#11-ghcr--acr-cutover-q4-deferred
troubleshooting | Troubleshooting | troubleshooting | 7-row symptom/cause/fix table: dotnet-format-drift, playwright-cache-miss, docker-layer-cache-cold, GHCR-403-on-fork-PR, frontend-coverage-empty, EF-Unable-to-bind-connection, ng-test-No-provider-for-Browser | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#12-troubleshooting
future-work | Future work | future | 7-row defer/tracking table: dogfooding-notify-hook (D1), frontend-lint ng-lint (D3), integration-smoke-e2e (Q12), GHCR->ACR (Q4), CD-ACA-revision-update (Q11), Trivy/SBOM, branch-protection-requires-CI-green | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#13-future-work